Sure! To customize the font size of the page header with the class `.header`, you can use the following CSS code:

```css
.header {
  font-size: 24px; /* You can adjust the size as needed */
}
```

### Explanation:
- `.header` selects the element with the class `header`.
- `font-size: 24px;` sets the font size to 24 pixels. You can change this value to any size you prefer (e.g., `1.5rem`, `1.2em`, `16px`, etc.).

### Example with other styling:
If you want to style the header in more detail, you can expand the CSS like this:

```css
.header {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  color: #333;
  text-align: center;
  margin: 20px 0;
}
```

